rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"How long should I wait before naming my new pet?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Most experts recommend waiting 2-5 days after bringing your pet home. This observation period lets you understand their personality, habits, and quirks before committing to a name. The name that feels right after a few days of bonding is usually the best choice.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Can I rename an adopted or rescue pet?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Absolutely! Adult pets can learn new names with patience and positive reinforcement. Use lots of treats, enthusiastic praise, and consistent repetition. Most pets adjust to a new name within 2-4 weeks. The key is always associating the new name with positive experiences.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Should my pet's name match their breed heritage?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"It's a personal choice with no right or wrong answer. Breed-heritage names (like 'Angus' for a Scottish Terrier or 'Sakura' for a Shiba Inu) add cultural meaning, but countless pets thrive with names that have no connection to their breed origins. Choose what resonates with you.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What if my family can't agree on a name?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Create a democratic process: each person nominates their top three names, create a combined shortlist, and vote. You can also try a tournament bracket where names compete head-to-head until a champion emerges. The key is giving everyone a voice while keeping the process fun.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Are two-word names practical?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Two-word names like 'Luna Mae' or 'Buddy Boo' can work beautifully, especially if you primarily use the first word for everyday calling and save the full name for formal moments. Consider whether both parts together roll off the tongue easily when called at a distance.\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"4e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"partridge\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/partridge/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\\\",\\\"ch